## System information\n\nN/A\n\n### Issue description\n\nA few of our `Container` nodes have special layout rules, whereby they stack children next to each other. In the current state of their layout code, this means they do not respect their children's desired sizes unless the child has the `SIZE_EXPAND` flag turned on. \nThis issue currently applies to `Label` and `TabBar` (and `TabContainer` by extension). Examples below use a `Label` with `OVERRUN_TRIM_CHAR`. \nThis issue is a limitation of #118651. \n\nSelf expanding `Label`:\n\n<img width=\"165\" height=\"89\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/19262de2-e40e-4bbf-9576-d90746c93d36\" />\n\nSame `Label` in a `BoxContainer`:\n\n<img width=\"32\" height=\"84\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a82f81ff-4af8-481b-a073-11adf548da20\" />\n\nSame `Label` in a `BoxContainer` with `SIZE_EXPAND` flag:\n\n<img width=\"157\" height=\"78\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bdd22145-4599-4f06-a727-8cffa0a22a84\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nTry it for yourself using the MRP.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nMRP has examples for `Label` and `TabBar` with the following conditions:\n* standalone\n* child of `PanelContainer` (working as it should, serves as positive example)\n* child of `BoxContainer`, `GridContainer`, and `FlowContainer` (not working as it should)\n\n[container-desired-sizes-mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27536876/container-desired-sizes-mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_